Date: Mon, 1 Mar 93 14:31:15 EST
From: eisrael@suneast.East.Sun.COM (Elias Israel - SunSelect Engineering)
Subject: BOMB: Who could have done this?

One question, touched upon by one person but not since explored, is who
might have bombed the WTC, how they might have done it, and for what
purpose.

Apparently, the FBI now claims to know for certain that it was a bomb
blast and not an accident. What I'd like to know is:

	(1) Whether that claim seems credible,
	(2) How much explosive would be required to cause the damage
	    that been reported,
	(3) Who could obtain access to the required materials,
	(4) Who could deliver the (reported) bomb to the garage,
	(5) What could  they hope to gain by the blast?

The answers to these questions that the news media have bandied about
don't seem to fit very well, unless you assume that the bomb was
planted by insane people.

That it was a bomb and not an accident seems plain to me, so I am
willing to accept that part of the claim.

How much explosive material would be required and who could obtain and
deliver it are questions that I cannot answer. However, it seems to me
that both activities require quite a bit of cash. Not the sort of thing
that ill-equipped foreign terrorists, fighting a grueling war of
attrition would be able to do easily, one imagines.

Finally, I find it hard to imagine how any military group, no matter
how crazed, could imagine that they would advance their cause by
attacking the US. History is quite clear on that lesson: attacking a
superpower, especially one that wants to remain uninvolved in your
personal conflicts, is a serious mistake.

So, the allegations presented so far don't seem to hang together for me
into a convincing story. Anyone got a better idea?

Elias Israel
eisrael@east.sun.com

