From: Brian.Hawthorne@East.Sun.COM (Brian Holt Hawthorne - SunSelect Engineering)
Subject: BOMB: Who could have done this?

The bomb did not actually require that much explosive power. Remember, 
it was planted at the bottom of a six story parking garage. All it had
to do was destroy enough of the structural members to knock out the 
floor above it. Gravity would do most of the rest. The "crater" may
have looked huge, but it was mostly empty space to begin with.

The FBI is currently saying it was "dynamite". This is readily available
to anyone in the construction industry, and isn't really tracked that
closely. It is also quite inexpensive.

I suspect nearly anyone could have parked a car in the garage, since 
garage security is often on the way out (although I don't know this
for a fact in the case of the WTC). Load up a car with dynamite, 
drive it to the bottom floor, set the timer and leave by the elevator. 

I have no idea why anyone would want to do it, or what they would hope
to gain (although you could make a profit on the havoc it wrought on the
commodities exchange, it would probably be noticed). Of course, I haven't
heard even the names of the (how many now?) 7 groups claiming responsibility.

Just imagine, if that had been a car loaded with fissionable material and
associated gadgetry instead of dynamite, though...

