What's a Humaneer?

 Good Question!  I define a Humaneer as anyone who believes that they can
make the world a better place for humanity as a whole and who is doing
something active and positive due to that belief.  If you are such a
person, then I'd like to hear about your experiences.  Humaneers are also
persons (in my definition) who are interested in alternative/progressive
issues and who are to some extent "early adopters" of technology because
they see its potential for increasing their creativity or furthuring
their goals in life.  Humaneers also believe deeply (hope for :)) in: 
racial/class equality,renewable energy, space exploration, global peace,
increasing human potential, computers as a means of communication and
bringing together persons from all over the world,and other issues
(Humaneers come from a variety of disciplines :)).  Humaneers don't just
sit around and wait for change, they take action! Humaneers are
innovative and creative. They are able to think for themselves and not be
part of the herd.  They may also be called entreprenurial.  But humaneers
aren't just in it for the money, they are persons who sincerely love what
they do and are engaged totally in their work as well as their play. 

I would like to create a directory or resource book for Humaneers, so
please let me know if you would like to be added to the list.

Thanks for taking the time to read this message.  I hope to hear from
some fellow humaneers!

