The events in Waco, Texas seem to bear on this. Here we have a household
which has what Mark wanted: isolated, critical mass of defenders, easily
defended approach path, and well-armed.

But the Feds decide they have to raid this household, putatively because of
"illegal arms" (never mind that nearly any arms, short of fully automatic
weapons, are quite legal in Texas...and fully automatic weapons, which I've
not heard were present, can also be legal if the right permits are held)
and because of "cult" activities.

Mark's household could just as easily be the target. He's advertised his
liking for guns and he belongs to this strange mind-altering cult called
"the Extropians." Some of these cult followers preach anarchy, and others
talk about giving their children nootropic drugs. I'd say a midnight raid
is in order!

This may bother some readers of this list, but here goes: When I hear the
details of why the raid was conducted, and then heard the final (up to now)
death toll of 5 Feds, 1 cult member, I actually cheered!

True, I feel sorry for their families, their friends, and even them (I
suppose), but viewing it more abstractly as a war between people who are
minding their own business on their own land and "the Feds," I'm glad the
Feds were killed.

(Sorry if this bothers some. I'll sit on this post for enough time to
reconsider my comments. If you are reading this, you can assume I coolly
considered it and decided to let it go out.)

Unless some substantive evidence of real criminal activity is produced,
I'll take the side of the so-called cultists.

-Tim, worrying that between the WTC bombing and the Waco shootout, new
crackdowns will be launched


